<title>CANADA: BC Tel union ratifies contract.</title>
<headline>BC Tel union ratifies contract.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>BC Telecom Inc said Monday that members of the Telecommunications Workers Union ratified a contract agreement with the phone company by an 88 percent margin.</p>
<p>The new contract provides a 2.25 percent wage increase retroactive to January 1, 1996; a 2.75 percent rise as of January 1, 1997; and a 3.25 percent raise in January 1998.</p>
<p>The company is also increasing some health and dental benefits and pension contributions. The union agreed to greater flexibility in work scheduling. The previous contract expired in December 1995.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
</text>
